{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"c2134d2a272c2dc9","type":"text","text":"**BIOLOGY**","x":980,"y":-10,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"92810fccad6675ae","type":"text","text":"**Blood types**\n\nClassification of your blood based on presense of certain [[Antigen|antigens]]\n\nYou can [[Heredity|inherit]] blood types from your parents. It must be noted that it is probablistic e.g. AA → A or O","x":1600,"y":964,"width":609,"height":194},
		{"id":"138901d2a42e49cf","type":"text","text":"[[Hormones]] are chemical messagers for the body\n\nControl\n- Chemical messages\n- Growth, metabolism, mood\n- Produced by glands of endocrine system","x":1689,"y":1298,"width":554,"height":270},
		{"id":"87e767b6d28d14ef","type":"text","text":"[[Antigen]] is any substance that your body views as harmful","x":2369,"y":880,"width":348,"height":84},
		{"id":"154dcac59557d164","type":"text","text":"Your body produces [[Antibody|antibodies]] to fight and destroy harmful substances\n\nY shape","x":2409,"y":1094,"width":380,"height":132},
		{"id":"39b9c74eefea09b3","type":"file","file":"01 Resources/Attachments/Pasted image 20260704115623.png","x":3009,"y":995,"width":400,"height":267},
		{"id":"22732b3de0eb31a3","type":"text","text":"Everything here right now is from my quick notepad on 2026-07-03. This shows how powerful a notepad is when you **act** on your notes","x":780,"y":205,"width":508,"height":122},
		{"id":"faff52322c36ab89","type":"text","text":"Proteins are made up of 4 structures, each more complex than the previous.\n\n**Primary**\n- Just pure [[Amino Acids]] in a polypeptide chain\n**Secondary**\nCan be of two shapes:\n1. Alpha helix (like [[DNA]])\n2. Beta sheet \nHeld by [[Hydrogen Bonding]]\n\n**Tertiary Structure**\nFolded chain containing both alpha and beta shapes of proteins\n\n**Quatenary Structure**\nMultiple folded chains, the most complex\n→[[Hemoglobin]]","x":-1800,"y":-1809,"width":859,"height":520},
		{"id":"1f6b89b908e127b7","type":"text","text":"A dehydration reaction between two amino acids of glycine","x":-1711,"y":-549,"width":342,"height":102},
		{"id":"9c39dcb2c256deb9","type":"text","text":"**Peptide Bonds**\n- Strong covalent bonds\n- Links each amino acid together\n- $-CNOH$ ","x":-1440,"y":-329,"width":420,"height":220},
		{"id":"90d0fa10559364e5","type":"text","text":"[[Amino Acids]] form peptides by condensation reactions (where a water molecule is lost). ","x":-1120,"y":-700,"width":382,"height":71},
		{"id":"e2f0b2b6d6b11815","type":"text","text":"Forces present in proteins","x":-1020,"y":-528,"width":250,"height":50},
		{"id":"54daffdada742e7d","type":"file","file":"01 Resources/Attachments/Pasted image 20260704114234.png","x":-1840,"y":-1059,"width":400,"height":301},
		{"id":"816b1bf0190c2cb3","type":"text","text":"[[Proteins]]","x":260,"y":-879,"width":160,"height":60},
		{"id":"9a9703277a14c5d5","type":"text","text":"Peptides are smaller chains of [[Amino Acids]] (2-50) which further make up proteins","x":-600,"y":-629,"width":362,"height":117},
		{"id":"f0d09b3ba033e6c9","type":"text","text":"[[Hydrogen Bonding|Hydrogen Bonds]]\n- Weak intermolecular forces\n- Reason why [[Proteins]] denature so easily (hydrogen bonds can be broken easily)","x":-800,"y":-249,"width":433,"height":168},
		{"id":"456421e6bc3c73eb","x":-419,"y":-874,"width":413,"height":111,"type":"text","text":"Made of 50+ [[Amino Acids]]. Proteins tend to carry out many different types of functions (e.g. Insulin regulates amount of glucose in blood)"},
		{"id":"9380db14dd7a0a27","type":"text","text":"Many [[Genes]] contain the genetic information on how to synthesise proteins","x":-385,"y":-1646,"width":382,"height":97},
		{"id":"705615b3c1f2ab12","type":"file","file":"01 Resources/Attachments/Pasted image 20260704114553.png","x":-640,"y":-1469,"width":346,"height":547},
		{"id":"5eaf464f242b34db","type":"text","text":"[[Genes]] are smaller sections of [[DNA]] which generally code for a specific function for something (e.g. eye colour)","x":2240,"y":-909,"width":364,"height":120},
		{"id":"175c96198cc1af46","type":"text","text":"[[DNA]] is a magnificent molecule in our body that contains the instructions for how an organism can function, reproduce, live and appear.","x":2264,"y":-590,"width":436,"height":122},
		{"id":"f38cbd829236321c","type":"file","file":"01 Resources/Attachments/Pasted image 20260704120308.png","x":2800,"y":-909,"width":289,"height":400}
	],
